            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Asphalt emulsion sealer typically lasts two to three years, coal tar four to five, and oil-based cutback sealers three to four. Those figures assume a properly applied two-coat job on a well-prepared surface. A thin single coat over poor preparation can wear through in a single season.",
          },
        },
